        <title>Explicit bounds for Buchstab&#39;s function</title>
            <categories>math.NT</categories>
            <comments>15 pages, 1 figure</comments>
            <msc-class>11N25, 34K25</msc-class>
            <license>http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/</license>
            <abstract>Buchstab&#39;s function $ω(u)$ describes the distribution of integers without small prime factors. We establish numerically explicit upper and lower bounds for $ω(u)$ that are easy to evaluate, without the need to solve the delay differential equation numerically.</abstract>
    </arXiv>

